    "q-116482": {
      "dom_id": "step-q116482",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "At a car rental agency, the charge $C,$ in dollars, for renting a car varies directly with the **square** of the distance  $d$ traveled by the car, measured in miles. If it costs $$5$ to rent a car to drive $20$ miles, then what equation models this situation?",
      "worked_solution": "The charge $C$ is directly proportional to the square of the distance $d,$ so we have\n\n$$\nC=k{d}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is the constant of variation.\n\nWe are told that $C=$5$ when $d=20\\,\\text{mi}.$ We can use this information to solve for $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =k\\cdot {20}^{2} \\\\ 5 & =k\\cdot 400 \\\\ \\frac{5}{400} & =k \\\\ \\frac{1}{80} & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our direct variation equation is\n\n$$\nC=\\frac{1}{80}{d}^{2}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
